Observe exact STOP and opted-in local UNI byte+FIN ACK.

Applies to picoquic 70b5fd5aafdd2d6c349ff783202ece9d778bcaf2, after 0001 to
0005.

Preserve callback values; append a successful send-commit event. Observation
is per existing local UNI, opt-in before sending, and retains no payload.
H3 forwards completion before releasing correlation; free is never success.
A STOP_SENDING received after the FIN is sent but before every byte and the
FIN are acknowledged is still delivered, and its signalled latch is set
before the callback runs. A stream with a requested reset is acknowledged
only once that reset is sent and acknowledged (and, for a reliable reset,
its prefix).

A reset accepted by picoquic_reset_stream_at wins over any later ACK: it
withdraws the stream's opt-in, so the committed callback never follows it.
The committed callback runs before picoquic_callback_stream_released, while
the stream's correlation is still live. PICOQUIC_STREAM_TERMINAL_CONTRACT_VERSION
advertises the contract.

Reset after FIN comes from upstream; 0003 retains terminal refusal and
context preservation, empty non-FIN ACK handling and reliable-prefix
retirement. This patch preserves reset precedence over a later FIN ACK.

Tests: adapters/picoquic/tests/test_pq_terminal.c in LibMoQ, with separate
constructed-state and deterministic native packet rows.

